    "outcomeVariants": {
      "strong": [
        "They would rather keep a tenant than find one. The number moves and the boiler gets serviced in the same week.",
        "You sit down with the account at the kitchen table in April, and what you pay for the place is what the place is worth. In October you could not have said that.",
        "You put bulbs in the window boxes in November, for a spring you already know you will be here to see.",
        "You end the season with something in writing that is better than what arrived in the envelope, on the two things you actually care about.",
        "The person who handles the building answers your email the same day, in one line, with the answer in it. Nothing in the fall worked like that."
      ],
      "solid": [
        "Signed without ceremony. The apartment costs a little more and asks nothing else of you.",
        "You stay, and the staying frees up the whole season for something that is not housing.",
        "The deposit you would have handed to somebody else stays where it is. You spend a little of it in February on the rug the front room has needed for years.",
        "You put up the shelves you had been holding off on in case you moved. They sit crooked in the corner and they hold everything you own.",
        "Two people in the building leave over the summer, and you are suddenly one of the ones who has been there a while. The man who fixes things knows your name."
      ],
      "poor": [
        "You spend the season looking, find nothing better at the money, and renew late on worse terms.",
        "The transfer goes up in October and stays up. You are paying more than you meant to for somewhere that is not better, and there is nothing left to try.",
        "The season goes on this, and the trip you had half-planned for the spring does not happen. Nobody chases you about it and it does not come back around.",
        "You look at what the listings want for places like yours, and yours is right in the middle of them. The years and the never being late are not on that page.",
        "The kitchen faucet goes in the winter and there is no goodwill anywhere to spend on getting it looked at. You pay someone to come out and mention it to nobody."
      ],
      "mixed": [
        "The month is thinner than last year's month. You go through the budget in October, move two things down the list to make it fit, and they stay down all year.",
        "The lease you end up signing has a paragraph about the carpets that nobody mentions out loud. You initial it, and it does not come up again.",
        "Someone at work asks whether you are settled now. You say yes, and spend the rest of the afternoon working out how true that was.",
        "The two boxes you never unpacked stay taped and stacked where they were. In April you put a third one on top of them.",
        "The chair that never fit anywhere still does not fit anywhere. By March you have stopped moving it around and started putting the laundry on it."
      ]
    },
